{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013gqXTshkKfDwEn5E76CTSU","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\"timestamp\":\"2026-07-18T14:15:00.000Z\",\"author\":\"coder-sonnet\",\"type\":\"blocked\",\"message\":\"FIX-004 code change complete in tools/roadmap-dashboard/index.html: added module-level const userSelections = new Map() (ticketId -> {runner, model}) near the other module-level state (REFRESH_MS/ticketsCache/allowlists). In buildCard(), before building the select options I read userSelections.get(ticket.id) into `saved`; after building runnerSelect's options I set runnerSelect.value = saved.runner if that value exists among the options; refreshModelOptions() (already responsible for rebuilding modelSelect when runner changes) now also restores modelSelect.value = saved.model if that value exists among the newly-built options (handles both the claude-model-list case and the disabled codex n/a case, since saved.model would be '' for codex and that option value is '' too). Added saveSelection() which writes {runner: runnerSelect.value, model: modelSelect.value} into the map, wired to modelSelect's 'change' event and combined into runnerSelect's existing 'change' listener (which still calls refreshModelOptions() first, then saveSelection()). No changes to REFRESH_MS, the poll mechanism, server.mjs, FIX-001's disabled-attribute logic, or FIX-003's isHumanTask badge branch (map lookup only happens inside the existing else-branch for non-human tickets). Manually re-read the full buildCard()/render() region after editing to confirm brace/paren balance and that the human-task branch is untouched. BLOCKED on verification only: this sandbox's Bash tool requires per-command human approval for every invocation attempted (`node --check tools/roadmap-dashboard/server.mjs`, a Function()-based inline-script syntax check via node -e, and `curl` against the running dashboard at 127.0.0.1:4570 were all rejected with 'This command requires approval/